  "oral_argument": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "3a92294cd28c949cf9d59e42f605c3c54777a29b4def462a40b5d38fc1a35989",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-3a92294cd28c-0000-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 6,
              "start": 6
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Ginsburg, jUSTICE GINSBURG: Mr. Bopp, would you clarify a procedural point? As I understand it, on the expenditure issue, there is no final decision that has gone back to the district court for further proceedings."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "3a92294cd28c949cf9d59e42f605c3c54777a29b4def462a40b5d38fc1a35989",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-3a92294cd28c-0000-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 9,
              "start": 9
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Kennedy, jUSTICE KENNEDY: Well, just --"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Souter",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "3a92294cd28c949cf9d59e42f605c3c54777a29b4def462a40b5d38fc1a35989",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-3a92294cd28c-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 21,
              "start": 21
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Souter, jUSTICE SOUTER: But on -- on your view, if -- if there were a -- a mandatory publicly funded scheme and the -- the limits on expenditure were very high -- it was a very generous scheme. They gave them lots of money -- it would still be unconstitutional because there would be -- I -- I take it on your view, because there would be an elimination of any way to participate by contributing. Is that correct?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "3a92294cd28c949cf9d59e42f605c3c54777a29b4def462a40b5d38fc1a35989",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-3a92294cd28c-0001-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 29,
              "start": 29
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Scalia, jUSTICE SCALIA: But that's the limit you've placed on -- on contributions."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "3a92294cd28c949cf9d59e42f605c3c54777a29b4def462a40b5d38fc1a35989",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-3a92294cd28c-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 39,
              "start": 39
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Scalia, jUSTICE SCALIA: If the burden is on the candidate to establish that -- that somebody's expenditure is independent and shouldn't be counted against his expenditure limit."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Souter",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "3a92294cd28c949cf9d59e42f605c3c54777a29b4def462a40b5d38fc1a35989",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-3a92294cd28c-0002-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 38,
              "start": 38
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "So the case is going back to the trial court on those bases anyway."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Vermont record",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "3a92294cd28c949cf9d59e42f605c3c54777a29b4def462a40b5d38fc1a35989",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-3a92294cd28c-0002-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 53,
              "start": 53
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "We had a record in Vermont that showed that for the previous nine election cycles before the act was enacted, only one incumbent had been defeated for a statewide office."
      }
    ],
